NAME
       vgextend - add physical volumes to a volume group

SYNOPSIS
       vgextend [-y] [-f] VG PV [PV...]

DESCRIPTION
       vgextend adds the space of more physical volumes to an existing volume
       group, without stopping anything. This is the first step when a
       logical volume must grow but its volume group has no free extents
       left: add a disk or partition to the VG, then lvextend the LV.

       Each PV argument may be a PV already, or a plain device; vgextend
       then initialises it as a PV first (as pvcreate would).

OPTIONS
       -y, --yes
              Answer yes to questions, such as wiping an old signature.

       -f, --force
              Go ahead without some checks.

EXAMPLES
       Add a new partition on /dev/vdc to vgdata, then grow an LV and its file
       system by 1 GiB:

           parted -s /dev/vdc mklabel gpt mkpart lvm 1MiB 100% set 1 lvm on
           pvcreate /dev/vdc1
           vgextend vgdata /dev/vdc1
           vgs vgdata
           lvextend -r -L +1G /dev/vgdata/lvdata

       Add a whole disk:

           vgextend vgdata /dev/vdc

NOTES
       Check the free space after extending with vgs (the VFree column) or
       vgdisplay (Free PE / Size).

SEE ALSO
       vgreduce(8), vgcreate(8), pvcreate(8), lvextend(8), vgs(8)
